From: HDSatelit <dev@hdsatelit.local>
Subject: [PATCH] JSC: keep the Map and Set fast iteration out of the 32-bit DFG

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [restore experimental ARM32 JIT]

The fast iteration protocol for Map and Set (for-of over a Map or a Set,
added after the ARMv7 JIT was disabled upstream) lowers iterator_open and
iterator_next to MapStorage and the map iteration nodes. Those nodes have
no JSVALUE32_64 backend: DFGSpeculativeJIT32_64.cpp answers MapStorage
with "unexpected node in DFG backend" and the process aborts as soon as
a function with such a loop reaches the DFG. The Map and Set intrinsics
of the bytecode parser already return early on 32-bit; the iteration
modes did not get that guard.

Drop the FastMap and FastSet modes on 32-bit exactly where the parser
already drops them when the iterator protocol watchpoint has fired: the
remaining modes are compiled, the generic path already checks that next
is an object, and with no mode left the code takes a forced OSR exit and
the loop runs in the baseline tier.
---
diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/dfg/DFGByteCodeParser.cpp b/Source/JavaScriptCore/dfg/DFGByteCodeParser.cpp
index 2430b94..fac6469 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/dfg/DFGByteCodeParser.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/dfg/DFGByteCodeParser.cpp
@@ -11610,13 +11610,14 @@ void ByteCodeParser::handleIteratorOpen(const JSInstruction* currentInstruction,
     }
     if (!globalObject->stringIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid())
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastString);
-    if (!globalObject->mapIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
+    // The Map and Set fast iteration modes lower to MapStorage, which has no JSVALUE32_64 backend.
+    if (!is64Bit() || !globalObject->mapIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMap);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMapKeys);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMapValues);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMapEntries);
     }
-    if (!globalObject->setIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
+    if (!is64Bit() || !globalObject->setIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastSet);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastSetValues);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastSetEntries);
@@ -12244,13 +12245,14 @@ void ByteCodeParser::handleIteratorNext(const JSInstruction* currentInstruction,
     }
     if (!globalObject->stringIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid())
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastString);
-    if (!globalObject->mapIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
+    // The Map and Set fast iteration modes lower to MapStorage, which has no JSVALUE32_64 backend.
+    if (!is64Bit() || !globalObject->mapIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMap);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMapKeys);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMapValues);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastMapEntries);
     }
-    if (!globalObject->setIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
+    if (!is64Bit() || !globalObject->setIteratorProtocolWatchpointSet().isStillValid()) {
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastSet);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastSetValues);
         seenModes &= ~static_cast<uint32_t>(IterationMode::FastSetEntries);
